Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 09:36:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(event-store): appends commit in global_nonce order, so a
 live subscriber cannot skip one (syntropic137#1545)

global_nonce is a BIGSERIAL: allocated at INSERT, visible at COMMIT. A slow
append holding nonce N while a faster one committed N+1 let a live subscriber
yield N+1, advance its cursor past N, and never deliver N. A per-tenant
transaction advisory lock taken before the first nonce is drawn makes the next
append wait until this one is visible.

it_commit_order reproduces it against real Postgres: without the lock the
subscriber delivers only N+1 (nonce 3 never arrives); with it, both in order.

Co-authored-by: Neural Empowerment <129192050+NeuralEmpowerment@users.noreply.github.com>
